      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T10:48:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you only update it when it\u0027s unset (so only set it here if it was 0L) ?\n\nThe idea is that lastSentTime is already updated on each query sent, but we just need a reasonable value for the first query. Because it\u0027s only used to calculate the minimum delay for the next query (it\u0027s always used as \"lastSentTime + baseDelay\"), using \"now\" effectively rates-limit the second query to now + baseDelay, which should be reasonable. \n\nWe don\u0027t need to raise the limit every time a new listener registers, so it doesn\u0027t need to be changed on every new listener.",
      "revId": "ad1acf8995575216d1c13199fb454b42ba989232",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
