      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T10:48:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually I realized that timeWhenScheduled and minRemainingTtlWhenScheduled are only used to calculate this. And this is equal to `minRemainingTtlWhenScheduled + timeWhenScheduled - now`\n\nSo instead of storing both `minRemainingTtlWhenScheduled` and `timeWhenScheduled`, you could just add them and store `minRemainingTtlWhenScheduled + timeWhenScheduled`, which could be called `lastScheduledTask.minTtlExpirationTimeWhenScheduled`.\n\nThat\u0027s only 1 value to keep instead of 2, and I think it\u0027s actually clearer.\n\nThen this check could be:\n\n`if (lastScheduledTask.minTtlExpirationTimeWhenScheduled \u003d\u003d now + minRemainingTtl)`\n\nI think that\u0027s also easier to understand as \"if the next TTL expiration time hasn\u0027t changed\"",
      "range": {
